course: dictionary
lesson: 6019
title: Meditate: calm mind and deep thought
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To meditate is to sit quietly and focus your mind, often on your breathing, so that you feel calm and peaceful. Meditate is a verb, so it changes: I meditate, she meditates, we meditated, they are meditating.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The Buddha taught the Four Noble Truths» is the start of the sentence, and the sentence goes on: «many Buddhists meditate to calm the mind.» Calm the mind tells you that meditate is about making the mind quiet and peaceful.
explain: The word has other meanings too. In religion, to meditate is to think deeply and prayerfully about God or a holy text. Formally, to meditate on something means to think about it seriously for a long time. Check which meaning fits by swapping your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Meditate means to sit quietly and focus your mind to feel calm.
fact: «Many Buddhists meditate to calm the mind.»
fact: Useful phrases are «meditate on» something, «meditate for ten minutes», and «guided meditation».
fact: In PSHE and well-being lessons, children may meditate or do mindfulness to calm worries and anger.
fact: In RE, pupils learn Buddhist meditation and Christian prayerful reading of the Psalms.
exercise: «Many Buddhists meditate to calm the mind.» What does meditate mean here? | To eat a big lunch | To shout loudly at a friend | To run very fast around the playground | *To sit quietly and focus the mind to feel calm
exercise: Priya says, «I will meditate on this problem for an hour.» What does meditate on mean? | *To think about it seriously for a long time | To forget it straight away | To throw it away | To draw a picture of it
exercise: In PSHE, the teacher says, «Let's meditate for ten minutes.» What should you do? | Shout your answers across the room | *Sit quietly and focus on your breathing | Run around the field
test: Which phrase means to think about something seriously for a long time? | Calm down right now | *meditate on it | Shout out loud
test: The dictionary says Buddhists, Hindus and Christians all meditate in their own ways. Which group is NOT named there? | Hindus | *Sikhs | Buddhists | Christians
exam: Which use of meditate is about religion? | We meditate on the bus to school | My dog likes to meditate in the garden with a ball | *Christians meditate on a holy text and think deeply about God | Meditate means to shout very loudly
